<title>USA: Sales of new homes unexpectedly strong in May.</title>
<headline>Sales of new homes unexpectedly strong in May.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales of new homes were unexpectedly strong in May, the Commerce Department said on Monday, jumping at the strongest rate in six months.</p>
<p>Sales climbed 7.1 percent to a seasonally adjusted annual rate of 825,000 units -- well above Wall Street economists' expectations of a 786,000-unit rate -- after a revised 8.1 percent fall in April. It was the strongest pickup in monthly sales since an 11.6 percent increase last November and brought the supply of new homes on the market down to its lowest in nearly 26 years.</p>
</text>
